  "narrative": "The response-deadline validation for H13 confirms the central TP53_loss association. H13 is the direction +1 weaker-dependency claim. Its independent validation estimate is +0.788 composite dependency-score units, with an independent interval of +0.698 to +0.878. This is highly consistent with the discovery estimate +0.829 [0.767,0.891], and the independent lower bound is far above the 0.15-unit scientific-meaningfulness threshold. Because the independent interval already accounts for the maximum validation burden, I accept H13 and close the main TP53_loss investigation. The earlier opposite-direction claim H1 remains rejected.\n\nThe newly delivered validation for H107 confirms the central SMARCA4_loss association. H107 is the direction -1 stronger-dependency claim: positive signed estimates mean SMARCA4_loss cells have more negative dependency_composite values, i.e. stronger composite dependency. The validation estimate is +0.823 units with independent interval +0.732 to +0.913, consistent with discovery estimate +0.804 [0.742,0.867]. Its lower bound is far above the 0.15-unit threshold. I accept H107 and close the main SMARCA4_loss investigation. The earlier H39 claim that SMARCA4_loss would associate with weaker dependency remains rejected; the validation evidence on that card is signed to the opposite hypothesis and further supports rejection.\n\nTogether with the previously validated KEAP1_loss claim H14, the currently strongest dataset-specific findings are: TP53_loss is associated with substantially weaker composite dependency (H13), KEAP1_loss is associated with substantially weaker composite dependency (H14), and SMARCA4_loss is associated with substantially stronger composite dependency (H107). These are observational associations in the supplied dataset. They should not be interpreted as causal effects or automatically generalizable beyond this dataset.\n\nNegative and boundary results remain important. The TP53-by-KEAP1 positive interaction claims H31 and H32 are unsupported; both estimate +0.077 [-0.042,0.196], below the threshold and statistically compatible with no interaction. The SMARCA4 technical and biological robustness checks are strong overall, but H128 does not support positive augmentation of the stronger-dependency SMARCA4 association in adenocarcinoma; it gives -0.174 [-0.312,-0.035], suggesting the opposite, namely attenuation of the stronger-dependency association in adenocarcinoma relative to the complement. The explicitly reversed attenuation claim H138, linked to the same R49 evidence, estimates +0.174 [0.035,0.312]. It is statistically nonzero and its point estimate exceeds 0.15, but its lower bound is below the threshold, so I treat it as unresolved rather than definitively meaningful without more evidence or validation. H129 and H132 do not support meaningful positive SMARCA4 interactions in batch_a or high Cas9 activity.\n\nThe main unresolved effect-size question is CDKN2A_loss. The reversed main claim H112 has discovery estimate +0.139 [0.065,0.213] in the stronger-dependency direction. It is statistically nonzero, but the point estimate is just below the 0.15-unit threshold and the interval spans subthreshold and threshold-exceeding values. Conditional CDKN2A analyses should decide whether this is a meaningful context-specific effect or a borderline null. Many broad predictors remain unanalyzed, including PTEN_loss, BRCA2_loss, NF1_loss, SMAD4_loss, BRAF_v600e, ERBB2_amplification, APC_mutation, MSI-high, sex, research marker F, and global omics availability contrasts. The most informative immediate next analysis is a CDKN2A-focused follow-up using the registered conditional CDKN2A claims, especially H120 through H123 together with the main near-threshold H112, to determine whether the CDKN2A signal exceeds the meaningfulness threshold in any biologically or technically interpretable stratum. After that, allocate further discovery to the still-untested broad predictor main effects to complete the landscape of dataset-specific associations.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration-4 synthesis update. H13 and H107 are now accepted and closed with independent validation. Supported dataset-specific central associations: TP53_loss weaker dependency (H13, validated); KEAP1_loss weaker dependency (H14, validated); SMARCA4_loss stronger dependency (H107, validated). All are observational and dataset-specific. Negative/rejected: H1, H2, H39 opposite-direction main claims; H31/H32 TP53xKEAP1 positive interaction; H128 positive SMARCA4 adenocarcinoma augmentation; H129 batch_a interaction; H132 high Cas9 interaction. Unresolved: CDKN2A main H112 near threshold, reversed stronger-dependency estimate +0.139 [0.065,0.213]; H138 attenuation of SMARCA4 stronger-dependency association in adenocarcinoma +0.174 [0.035,0.312] because lower bound below threshold. Many broad predictor claims remain unanalyzed: H23, H24, H38, H41-H45, H70, H71, H76 and related interactions. Immediate next analysis priority: CDKN2A conditional H120-H123 plus H112 to resolve near-threshold signal. Secondary priorities: SMARCA4 conditional main claims H108-H111 and interactions H118-H119/H130-H137 if capacity; then broad untested main predictors. No new validation requested this stage; H107 validation already completed. Keep all claims dataset-specific, not causal/generalizable."
